Viewer log: how far the picture lags behind (2026-10-12).

On the road some wired sessions lagged for their first ten-odd seconds and a replug cured it. The box's
per-viewer send queue holds 1024 messages and drops only when full, so a slow moment on the car's Wi-Fi
turns into lag instead of skipped frames. The page now pings once a second while CarPlay runs; the pong
waits behind every queued frame, and the worst round trip of each 10-second report (a pong still on its
way counts with its age) goes to the box log as lagMs.

